1
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:42,000
Billy's Balloon is a animation, comedy, thriller
film directed by Don Hertzfeldt.

2
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:18,000
A balloon wraps itself around a young child's hand, bringing him higher and higher,
much to the child's delight, but a sinister truth begins to unravel.

3
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:54,000
Billy's Balloon is a 16 mm animated short by Don Hertzfeldt.

4
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:30,000
It was his fourth and final student film at UC Santa Barbara.

5
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:06,000
Similar to his other cartoons, he uses a minimalist stick-figure technique.

6
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:42,000
The film was invited into Official Competition at the 1999 Cannes Film Festival (where Hertzfeldt was the
youngest director involved), and it won the Grand Jury Award at the 1999 Slamdance Film Festival.

7
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:18,000
On top of its film festival runs (and subsequent popularity online), the short has also appeared on Adult
Swim and MTV in the US and on a number of international TV broadcasts around the world.

8
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:54,000
Hertzfeldt has noted that the short's international popularity is likely
because it has no dialogue and plays like a silent film.

9
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:30,000
The tone is lighthearted and intense.
